---
import Layout from '@boring-sites/design/Layout.astro';
import NoLogsBanner from '../components/NoLogsBanner.astro';
const siteName = 'What Is My IP';
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About What Is My IP — the privacy-first IP lookup tool."
  siteName={siteName}
>
  <NoLogsBanner />
  <article class="container-prose py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-8 dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        <strong>What Is My IP</strong> is a small, privacy-respecting IP lookup tool. It's part of the
        <a href="https://github.com/ksjpswaroop/boring-sites">boring-sites</a> portfolio — a collection of small utility sites built with the same design system.
      </p>
      <h2>The trust claim</h2>
      <p>
        The site detects your public IP and displays it. We <strong>do not store it</strong> on any server, in any database, or in any analytics system. The claim is verifiable in three ways:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explicitly states what we don't collect.</li>
        <li>The <a href="https://github.com/ksjpswaroop/boring-sites">source code is open source</a> — you can audit every byte that runs on the server.</li>
        <li>The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> explains the technical setup (Vercel Edge Functions, no DB, no Google Analytics).</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>What we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> — cookieless, GDPR-compliant, no IP storage. We use it to count visits, that's all.</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — for ads. AdSense may set cookies for ad personalization. Opt out at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party trackers</strong>. No Facebook Pixel, no Google Analytics, no Hotjar, no Mixpanel.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we don't use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No Google Analytics (it stores IPs).</li>
        <li>No server-side logging of request IPs.</li>
        <li>No database.</li>
        <li>No authentication, no accounts, no saved state on our side.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        The category leader (<a href="https://whatismyip.com" rel="nofollow">whatismyip.com</a>) is a 2003-era page with a "share my IP with advertisers" business model. We built this as the alternative: the same utility, with a privacy story that's actually true.
      </p>
      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> on <a href="https://vercel.com">Vercel</a> Edge Functions. Styled with <a href="https://tailwindcss.com">Tailwind CSS</a>. Analytics by <a href="https://plausible.io">Plausible</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
